{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgk8LzAXfwMHMhPFfQBKx", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Short answer:** Two services call the NotificationsAPI directly: **BillingService** and **PaymentsService**. If the notifications Redis instance goes down, neither can get messages delivered. The graph doesn't say what happens to a message after all its retries fail.\n\n**Why Redis takes both callers down**\n- **NotificationsService** exposes the **NotificationsAPI**.\n- NotificationsService keeps its data in the **NotificationsRedisInstance** (a STORES relationship). That's the only dependency the graph lists for it, so losing Redis cuts off the one place it stores data.\n- **BillingService** and **PaymentsService** both call NotificationsAPI directly, so both lose message delivery.\n\n**Services hit indirectly (they don't call NotificationsAPI themselves):**\n- **RenewalsWorker**, through its dependency on BillingService\n- **ReportingService**, through its dependency on BillingService\n- **OrderService**, which calls **PaymentsAPI** (exposed by PaymentsService), which then calls NotificationsAPI\n\n**Retries**\n- NotificationsService makes three attempts with a 250ms backoff. The config key **RETRY_ATTEMPTS** controls this, and it applies only to NotificationsService.\n- The graph has nothing on what happens to a message after the third attempt fails. There's no dead-letter queue, fallback store, alert, or caller-side handling. It may simply be dropped, but the graph doesn't confirm that. To find out, you'd need to check NotificationsService's code or runbook.\n- Also, it's unclear whether retries would help at all with Redis gone. If the retries depend on Redis themselves, all three attempts will likely fail in quick succession, about 750ms in total."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 677, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5265, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 677}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "847eb3c7-0d28-4df1-a4de-da5e336b735f", "uuid": "fc85c086-aee0-4bed-8fa4-4b3097f81a9a", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T16:51:51.317Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgk8LywshXJwRsi8Y5VCw"}
